  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A teacher wants to estimate the standard deviation of some students' grades on the final math exam. The following frequency table records the students' grades.\n\n| Grades (${x}_{i}$) | Frequency $({f}_{i})$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $50\\le x<60$ | $2$ |\n| $60\\le x<70$ | $5$ |\n| $70\\le x<80$ | $10$ |\n| $80\\le x<90$ | $6$ |\n| $90\\le x<100$ | $5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThe estimated mean grade is $\\overset{―}{x}≈77.5.$ Using the midpoint of each class interval to approximate all observations within that class, estimate the standard deviation ${\\sigma }_{n},$ using $n$ as the denominator in the variance formula.\n\nRounded to one decimal place, ${\\sigma }_{n}≈$\n{{field-1}}.",
